'' THE OTHER HALF of mt-define.test: with no '-mt', __FB_MT__ is 0 and the '#if'
'' arm is not taken. Without this the first test would still pass if the define
'' were hard-coded to -1 -- which is exactly the shape of the bug it replaced,
'' only inverted.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0309
'' EXPECT-NOT: threading is on

#if __FB_MT__
#error threading is on
#endif
print "reached"
